<!DOCTYPE html><html lang="en"><head><meta charset="utf-8"><title>Hello, TSX on the server · Velt blog</title></head><body><header><a href="/">Velt blog</a></header><main><article><h1>Hello, TSX on the server</h1><p class="meta">Ada · 2026-09-30</p><p>This blog is rendered by Velt from TSX components: the same syntax a browser app uses, compiled to native code with the markup folded into constant strings.</p><p>Components are plain functions of their props. The server streams each page, so the top of it reaches the browser while the comments still load.</p><ul class="tags"><li><a href="/?tag=tsx">#tsx</a></li><li><a href="/?tag=velt">#velt</a></li></ul></article><section class="comments"><h2>3 comments</h2><ul><li><b>Grace</b>: Nice and fast.</li><li><b>Linus</b>: Does it stream?</li><li><b>Ada</b>: It does: the comments you&#x27;re reading came last, after a &quot;slow&quot; query.</li></ul></section></main><footer>Rendered on the server with TSX</footer></body></html>
